--- SURFACE DESIGN (parity with the web source) ---
WinUI 3 ContentDialog (TsModal) with two render modes, exactly mirroring the web component:
  INPUT mode  : TsTabs (From File / Paste JSON / From URL) + a transient parse-error TsInlineCallout.
                - File : drag-and-drop zone (StorageItems) + Browse button backed by a .json FileOpenPicker.
                - Paste: monospace TsTextarea + "Validate & Preview".
                - URL  : share-link TsInput + "Load from URL".
  PREVIEW mode: error / warning TsInlineCallouts; a validated-dashboard summary (reused MiniGridPreview
                thumbnail + name + available/skipped TsBadges) OR a TsEmptyState ("Cannot preview this
                layout"); the widget-availability list; and Back / Import actions.
Every web state branch is reproduced: input, the 5 parse errors (emptyInput / readError / invalidFileType /
noImportParam / invalidUrl), auto-validate-on-open (initialJson), preview-valid, preview-with-errors and the
"cannot preview" empty state. The web component performs NO network read (its only hook is useTranslation),
so there is no loading / stale / offline branch — consistent with the web source and noted per the prompt's
state matrix.

Architecture (matches the established native modal pattern, e.g. FeedbackModal / NotificationBellPopover):
  - ImportPreviewModal.Model.cs   : WinUI-free. ImportValidator (port of validateImportData + URL decode +
                                    URL-safe base64 + .json drop guard), ImportValidation / ImportedDashboard /
                                    ImportLayoutItem records, ImportWidgetRegistry (availability resolved
                                    against the shared WidgetPickerCatalog = native WIDGET_REGISTRY),
                                    ImportPreviewRegistration (i18n keys + Segoe glyphs), ImportPreviewProjection
                                    (tabs / error lines / widget rows / MiniGridPreview model), diagnostics.
  - ImportPreviewModal.Source.cs  : WinUI-free. IImportFilePicker seam + StaticImportFilePicker fake.
  - ImportPreviewModal.ViewModel.cs: WinUI-free INotifyPropertyChanged state holder (all web useState + the
                                    validate / url / file / back / confirm / close transitions).
  - ImportPreviewModal.cs         : the WinUI 3 view + the concrete window-backed WindowImportFilePicker
                                    (FileOpenPicker initialized with App.MainWindow's HWND). Exercised by the
                                    app build.
i18n: every visible string flows through the ILocalizer (P1/S10) facade with the verbatim web key + English
fallback (import.title / import.preview / import.fromFile / import.fromClipboard / import.fromUrl /
import.dropFile / import.browse / import.fileInput / import.validate / import.loadUrl / import.widgets /
import.notAvailable / import.cannotPreview / import.back / import.confirm / import.availableCount /
import.missingCount / import.emptyInput / import.readError / import.invalidFileType / import.noImportParam /
import.invalidUrl + common.close). The validator's English findings (web inline literals) are keyed under
import.error.* / import.warning.* so no inline English ships. NOTE: the native Strings/{ar,en,he}/Resources.resw
catalog uses a separate flat `translation.*` scheme; NO surface's dotted keys (feedback.* / notifications.* /
import.* / common.*) live there — every surface resolves them via the ILocalizer facade + English fallback.
This surface follows that established, accepted pattern (identical to FeedbackModal, which is DONE).

